PRE-EXISTING BACKEND DEFECT (NOT introduced by this batch) — found while QA-ing NEARS-1041.

Admin/config/filesystems.php:42
    'url' => env('APP_URL').'storage',        <-- no '/' separator

Admin/.env:5
    APP_URL=http://localhost

=> Storage::disk('public')->url('banner/d-5bed135c7c.png')
   yields:  http://localhoststorage/banner/d-5bed135c7c.png
                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ host "localhoststorage" — unresolvable

LIVE PROOF (GET /api/v1/banners, zoneId:[1], moduleId:1, default env):
  id=1  full=http://127.0.0.1:8000/public/assets/admin/img/900x400/img1.jpg
  id=18 full=http://localhoststorage/banner/d-5bed135c7c.png     <-- BROKEN
  id=19 full=http://localhoststorage/banner/d-761b162ee9.png     <-- BROKEN
  id=20 full=http://localhoststorage/banner/d-4269c5d085.png     <-- BROKEN
  id=27 full=http://localhoststorage/banner/d-5bed135c7c.png     <-- BROKEN
  id=28 full=http://127.0.0.1:8000/public/assets/admin/img/900x400/img1.jpg

IMPACT: every image served from the `public` storage disk (banner/, store/,
store/cover/, product/, category/) is unfetchable from a device. The app's
CustomImage._normalizeHost only rewrites hosts '127.0.0.1' and 'localhost',
so 'localhoststorage' is passed through and fails DNS -> branded placeholder.
This is why 4 of 6 zone-1 banners render as placeholders in a default dev env.

NOT a local-only misconfig: the concatenation is broken for ANY APP_URL that
does not end in '/'. e.g. APP_URL=https://api.nears.app -> "https://api.nears.appstorage".
It only works by accident when APP_URL has a trailing slash.

QA WORKAROUND USED (no file/DB writes): ran the primary-tree backend with an
env override `APP_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8020/` (trailing slash) so all six banner
URLs were well-formed and the NEARS-1041 fix could be tested at full fidelity.
